    question: 'What is the main difference between Medigap Plan G and Plan N?',
    answer: 'Both plans cover the 20% Medicare Part B coinsurance and the $1,736 Part A deductible. Plan G covers 100% of all medical bills after you pay the annual $283 Part B deductible. Plan N offers 20–30% lower monthly premiums, but requires up to $20 copays for office visits, $50 for ER visits, and does not cover Part B excess charges.',
